You only provided the model syntax and warning message, so it is difficult to tell whether you specified the lavaan() call correctly.  If there was no error message, then perhaps it is still possible to request ICCs via lavInspect(fit, "icc") to verify that there is indeed variance at both levels for all the variables you specified at both levels.  If there is very little variance at a level, then that can cause problems.

A wide-format approach would not be out of the question, but it would be quite a large model.

